    "/api/v2/policies/search/": {
      "post": {
        "operationId": "Search_4",
        "description": "TODO:\n* Couple of potential problems with this method:\n    - The `next()` call will throw a StopIteration if the generator is empty\n    - The way we're using `most_recent_evaluations_per_policy` might end up being expensive memory-wise (and db-wise),\n    might be better to use a `Subquery` or `OuterRef` to get the most recent evaluation. Actually, I'm not even sure why\n    we're not just using the `PolicyEvaluation` queryset directly, filtering and annotating in place, would likely be\n    safer.\n* I removed a queryset that was unused, but I'm confused why it was there in the first place, merits investigation\n\nWill address this in future commits.",
        "tags": [
          "policies"
        ],
        "requestBody": {
          "content": {
            "application/json": {
              "schema": {
                "$ref": "#/components/schemas/PolicyRequest"
              }
            },
            "application/x-www-form-urlencoded": {
              "schema": {
                "$ref": "#/components/schemas/PolicyRequest"
              }
            },
